# Check out LF on every platform, Windows included. Without this a Windows
# runner gets CRLF, and `prettier --check` (whose endOfLine default is lf)
# then fails on every file. It also keeps any newline-sensitive comparison
# in the tests and in the generated snippets platform-independent.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binary content.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
